 "applies_to": "Each configured load (virtual BACnet device) of the Johnson Controls EEM multi-circuit electric energy meter.",
 "summary": "Every load configured on the EEM multi-circuit meter appears as its own virtual BACnet device. Its objects give the load voltages and frequency, totals for real, reactive and apparent power, power factor, demand, peak demand and energy (import, export and per quadrant), and a per-CT block of current, power, energy and phase angle, plus a CT polarity correction.",
 "notes": [
  "Objects from the Load Device(s) Object List, pages 2-4 of LIT-12013610.",
  "The meter shows up as a root device plus one virtual BACnet device per configured load; the two object lists are separate library entries.",
  "The object list has no access column. Access is inferred: measurements read-only; the guide notes the phase angle units can be written (radians or degrees-phase).",
  "Network settings in the integration notes come from the EEM Multi-Circuit Installation and Operation Manual (LIT-12013609) on the same portal.",
  "Only the first CT (phase L1) block is listed: AI 31-53 and BV 1. The guide reserves AI 60-82 and BV 2 for the second CT and AI 90-112 and BV 3 for the third CT of a load; their names are not printed.",
  "BV 1 Polarity Correction is marked writable by inference."
 ],
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Choose BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP in the meter web portal, give each configured load a unique virtual device instance, then discover the load devices and read real power, energy, demand and current.",
