   {
    "ref": "AI 8",
    "name": "Total Real Power (kW)",
    "why": "Total real power, kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 18",
    "name": "Total Kilowatt Hours (kWh)",
    "why": "Total energy, kWh"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 17",
    "name": "Total Present Demand",
    "why": "Present demand, kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 15",
    "name": "Total Peak Demand (PD)",
    "why": "Peak demand, kW"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 9",
    "name": "Total Amperage (A)",
    "why": "Total current, A"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1",
    "name": "Line 1 Measured Line-Neutral Voltage (L1-N)",
    "why": "L1-N voltage, V"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 11",
    "name": "Total Apparent Power Factor (aPF)",
    "why": "Apparent power factor, -1 to 1"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 7",
    "name": "Frequency",
    "why": "Frequency, Hz"
   }
  ],
  "enable": null,
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Protocol is chosen in the meter's web portal: BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, Modbus RTU or Modbus TCP.",
   "BACnet settings: base device instance (0 to 4194328 per the manual), base device name, virtual network number; BACnet IP adds UDP port and BBMD address/TTL; BACnet MS/TP adds MAC 0 to 127, Max Master and Max Info Frames.",
   "MS/TP baud rates 9600, 19200, 38400 (default), 57600 and 76800; 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit.",
   "Each configured load gets its own virtual device instance (VDI); the manual says to give every load a unique VDI."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "After choosing BACnet, give every load its own VDI; the manual says this is needed for reliable network performance.",
   "AI 52 (CT 1 kvarh delivered) is noted as Q1+Q3 in the guide while the load total AI 29 is Q1+Q2; check which applies.",
   "Root and load devices reuse the same AI instance numbers; map them by device."
  ]
 },
